338	    <span class="bar-val">${Number(value).toFixed(1)}</span>
339	  </div>`;
340	}
341	
342	function defaultWhy(r) {
343	  const c = r.components;
344	  const top = Object.entries({shipped: c.shipped_scope, leverage: c.leverage_on_others, stewardship: c.domain_stewardship})
345	    .sort((a,b) => b[1]-a[1])[0][0];
346	  const label = { shipped: 'broad structural reach across shared code', leverage: 'high review leverage helping teammates ship', stewardship: 'sustained activity across multiple subsystems' }[top];
347	  return `Ranks strongly on ${label}.`;
348	}
349	
350	function toggleCard(button) {
351	  const card = button.closest('.card');
352	  const expanded = card.classList.toggle('expanded');
353	  button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(expanded));
354	}
355	
356	function renderRankings() {
357	  const cfg = metricConfig[activeMetric];
358	  const ranked = [...currentData.rankings].sort((a, b) => cfg.value(b) - cfg.value(a) || a.login.localeCompare(b.login));
359	  const top10 = ranked.slice(0, 10);
360	  document.getElementById('cards').innerHTML = top10.map((r, i) => cardHTML(r, i + 1, (currentData.why_overrides || {})[r.login])).join('');
361	  document.getElementById('cutline').textContent = `Showing the top 10 by ${cfg.label.toLowerCase()}. Select another component to re-rank.`;
362	}
363	
364	function render(data) {
365	  currentData = data;
366	  document.getElementById('methodology-line').textContent = data.meta.methodology;
367	  document.getElementById('freshness').textContent =
368	    `${data.meta.total_prs.toLocaleString()} merged PRs from ${data.meta.eligible_engineers} engineers analyzed, ` +
369	    `${data.meta.window_start} to ${data.meta.window_end}. ` +
370	    `${data.meta.bot_authored_prs_excluded} bot-authored and ${data.meta.mechanical_prs_excluded} mechanical PRs excluded from scoring.`;
371	
372	  renderRankings();
373	
374	  document.getElementById('method-body').innerHTML = `
375	    <div>
376	      <h4>Shipped Scope / Blast Radius — 45%</h4>
377	      <p>Co-touch centrality: for every merged PR, we count how many <em>other</em> engineers also touched the same files elsewhere in the 90-day window, take the <strong>mean damped weight across that PR's files</strong>, then take the <strong>mean across each engineer's PRs</strong>. Both levels are averages, so a PR does not score higher merely because it contains more files, and the component is not won by whoever merged the most PRs. It is a proxy for engineering blast radius, not a claim about customer or revenue impact. Mechanical PRs (lockfile-only diffs and dependency bumps) are excluded from scored components.</p>
378	      <h4>Leverage on Others — 35%</h4>
379	      <p>Substantive reviews given to other engineers' PRs (state APPROVED/CHANGES_REQUESTED with a non-trivial comment body — rubber-stamp approvals don't count), multiplied by <code>log1p</code> of the number of distinct teammates reviewed. There is no speed modifier because GitHub does not provide a reliable request-to-first-review interval for resolved requests. Review connections are fully paginated; GitHub Apps and automated tools are excluded by actor type and known-account markers.</p>
380	    </div>
381	    <div>
382	      <h4>Domain Stewardship — 20%</h4>
383	      <p>PR titles are parsed for their conventional-commit scope (e.g. <code>feat(scope): …</code>); when a title has no scope (${data.meta.scope_fallback_pct}% of PRs), we fall back to the dominant top-level directory of the changed files. Within each scope, the top-2 most active engineers by authored + substantive reviewed activity earn stewardship credit. This shows sustained activity around an area; it does not claim work was actively routed to that person.</p>
384	      <h4>Evidence confidence &amp; ranking</h4>
385	      <p>Every engineer with at least one qualifying contribution is ranked — there is no minimum-activity cutoff, so someone who shipped one large piece of infrastructure and spent the rest of the window reviewing can still surface. The confidence label shows how much evidence backs the number; it affects how a score should be <em>read</em>, never the ranking itself. All three components are percentile-ranked (not min-max normalized) across the eligible engineer set so a single volume outlier can't compress everyone else's score.</p>
386	    </div>`;
387	
388	  document.getElementById('footer').textContent =
389	    `Source: PostHog/posthog · Generated ${new Date(data.meta.generated_at || Date.now()).toISOString().slice(0,16).replace('T',' ')} UTC · Ranking is fully deterministic (Python); no LLM in the scoring path.`;
390	}
391	
392	document.querySelectorAll('.metric-controls button').forEach(button => {
393	  button.addEventListener('click', () => {
394	    activeMetric = button.dataset.metric;
395	    document.querySelectorAll('.metric-controls button').forEach(b => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b === button)));
396	    renderRankings();
397	  });
398	});
399	
400	main();
401	</script>
402	</body>
403	</html>
